{"name":"Bronze Satin","hex":"#cc5533","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bronze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring or man-made alloy of copper, usually in combination with tin, but also with one or more other metals.","A reddish-brown colour, the colour of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of bronze metal.","Having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze"},{"term":"satin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cloth woven from silk, nylon or polyester with a glossy surface and a dull back. (The same weaving technique applied to cotton produces cloth termed sateen).","Gin (the drink)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Semigloss."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/satin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, ductility, or machinability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg/330px-Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze","wikidata":"Q34095"},{"title":"Satin","blocks":[{"text":"A satin weave is a type of fabric weave that produces a characteristically glossy, smooth or lustrous material, typically with a glossy top surface and a dull back; it is not durable, as it tends to snag. It is one of three fundamental types of textile weaves alongside plain weave and twill weave."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Satin_weave_in_silk_90.jpg/330px-Satin_weave_in_silk_90.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satin","wikidata":"Q14298"},{"title":"Bronze (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is a metallic brown color which resembles the metal alloy bronze. An archaic term for it was aeneous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png/330px-Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_(color)","wikidata":"Q2778382"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEgypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_19